# Deploy Workflow

**NEVER use `git commit`, `git add`, or `git push` directly in this repo.**

When the user asks to commit, deploy, push, or publish changes, always run:

```sh
sh deploy.sh
```

This single script: builds VitePress (`yarn docs:build`), commits the dist output, and pushes to GitHub, which triggers the upstream GitHub Actions pipeline automatically.

## Why
`deploy.sh` operates on the built `docs/.vitepress/dist/` subtree, not the source tree. Running `git commit` on the source would skip the build and break the published site.

## Checklist before deploying
- Verify all file edits are saved.
- Run `yarn docs:build` mentally — `deploy.sh` will do it, but flag any known build errors first.
- Then run `sh deploy.sh` from the repo root.

## Site structure reminder
The homepage (`docs/index.md`) is a **project gallery first**. Project tiles come before the Notes tile. When adding content, default to a new project tile rather than a notes entry unless the user specifically asks for a note.
